# L1 hosted agent service (src/hosted-main.ts). Copy to env/l1-hosted.env. Never add the payer key here (INV-3).
NETWORK=local
SELLER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4021
CONTROL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4020
SETTLEMENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:4023
# local only
CONTROL_TOKEN=dev-control-token
# local only
VERIFIER_TOKEN=dev-verifier-token
# foundry (managed identity, Azure) or anthropic (API key)
MODEL_PROVIDER=anthropic
# set me (anthropic only; forbidden with foundry)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# optional; default claude-sonnet-5-5 (allow-list in specs/011 contracts/model-access.md)
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=
# foundry only: https://<resource>.services.ai.azure.com/anthropic/v1
# FOUNDRY_BASE_URL=
# foundry only: client ID of the agent's user-assigned identity
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
# Callers come from one issuer, the sign-in tenant (016, SPEC L1-6): a person with the permission agent:run from one
# of the agent's clients, or a machine caller (client credentials) with that permission from its grant. All three
# are required. The tenant's values are Terraform's output l1_env (auth0/): the issuer https://<domain>/ with the
# final slash, people's API's identifier and the agent's clients. The local dev issuer uses urn:x402:dev-issuer,
# api://x402-l1-agent and x402-agent-cli-dev,x402-agent-desktop-dev
AUTH_ISSUER=urn:x402:dev-issuer
AUTH_AUDIENCE=api://x402-l1-agent
# the clients a person's token may come from, comma-separated. Never the portal's client: the service refuses to
# start with PORTAL_CLIENT_ID on this list. A machine caller's client is not listed. 019: the docs page's client and
# the desktop client (a person signs in from their own computer: browser, loopback return, PKCE)
AGENT_CLIENT_IDS=x402-agent-cli-dev,x402-agent-desktop-dev
# AUTH_TENANT_ID and SERVICE_AUDIENCE (the organization's directory) are no longer used: the service refuses to
# start while either is set
# local only: the dev issuer's JWKS from `npm run dev-token`. Remove it to accept the tenant's tokens
AUTH_JWKS_FILE=.local/dev-issuer/jwks.json
# optional, with API_DOCS=1 and the tenant (not the dev issuer): the client the docs page signs people in through.
# One of AGENT_CLIENT_IDS
# API_DOCS_CLIENT_ID=
# optional, 019, with the tenant (not the dev issuer): the desktop client. Set, GET /.well-known/agent-auth serves the
# sign-in settings a desktop client needs; it must be one of AGENT_CLIENT_IDS. Terraform's output l1_env prints it
# AGENT_DESKTOP_CLIENT_ID=
# set me: 32+ random bytes, hex or base64 (openssl rand -hex 32)
SESSION_REF_SECRET=
# optional, 013: the portal's client at the tenant, only to refuse a start with it on AGENT_CLIENT_IDS (SEC-20)
# PORTAL_CLIENT_ID=
# optional; default 4024
# AGENT_PORT=
# optional; default 127.0.0.1 (containers set 0.0.0.0). v1.27: with AUTH_JWKS_FILE it must be a loopback address,
# and TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS 0, or the service refuses to start (the dev sign-in serves this machine only)
# AGENT_BIND_HOST=
# optional; default 0. How many reverse proxies stand in front (1 behind the Azure ingress): the per-address
# request limit then counts the client's address from X-Forwarded-For. Never set it when nothing is in front.
# TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=
# optional: 1 serves Swagger UI at /docs with no token (docs/l1-hosted.openapi.yaml); off by default, never in Azure
# API_DOCS=1
# 021: the agent's mode. 1 is test mode: the agent goes straight to SELLER_URL's catalog, as before 021. 0 (or
# absent) is search mode: it may search the public x402 discovery index first. Any other value stops the agent. The
# local chain has no public index, so this example sets test mode
AGENT_TEST_MODE=1
# search mode only: the index's search address. Default on base-sepolia: the public index (Coinbase's Bazaar); on
# local there is none, and search mode without it refuses to start. https, or http to a loopback host on local
# DISCOVERY_URL=
